  "title": "Compressed attention projections do not imply a compressed runtime KV cache",
  "mechanism": "The pinned DeepSeek V2 implementation expands compressed KV through kv_b_proj, combines non-RoPE and rotated key components, pads Q/K/V to a common head size, and stores the expanded keys and values. Its attention then separates prefill and paged decode. Gemma2 selects sliding layers by parity; Gemma3 uses sliding_window_pattern and per-layer rotary bases, with explicit masks consumed by its non-flashinfer SDPA prefill branch. GPT-2 instead adds learned position embeddings.",
